A||N||5||SloPonti||A little Help With A Few Sunroof Questions!!!||||5||
Z||000000||SloPonti||05-12-2000||12:24 AM||||i have an 84 coupe with out a sunroof! i would like to add the sunroof option but my car has already been repainted and i prefer not to add a new top to the fiero! well tonight i had the headliner out and i notice the space were the sunroof cutout should be! i was wondering if i were to cut it out and get a new sunroof seal and a factory sunroof and a new headliner if i could just cutout my roof and install the factory one this way! it would be easier i think! i have all the tools to cut it- not worried about that part but just want to make sure that this can be done!<BR>thanks guys and gals!!<BR>Rob<BR>check out picture of roof! <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/roof1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/roof1.jpg</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||05-12-2000||12:33 AM||||Nope the channel that holds the seal is part of the roof panel and not something that can be added||||reg||1
Z||000002||007DOUG||05-12-2000||12:38 AM||||Since you don't want to repaint, you could always add an aftermarket sunroof. They can be installed without screwing up you paint.<P>Then, if you don't like the aftermarket, you can always add a factory sunroof (with alot of work)||||reg||1
Z||000003||SloPonti||05-12-2000||12:42 AM||||what would it take to add this channel? the factory had to do it somehow! how can i do it! or can i do it!<BR>thnaks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-12-2000||01:47 AM||||The amount of time it would take to fiberglass in a channel for the sunroof would be not worth it and you'd still have to repaint the roof. Just get a new roof, have it painted then swap. The factory sunroof swap only takes 2 hours to do and to paint the new roof would cost probably under $100. (The body shop I use is going to paint my new hood for $75) An aftermarket sunroof would be another way to go but it would never be as large as the stock one.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierodave||05-12-2000||04:03 AM||||Rob if you no longer want me to hold the sunroof section for you please let me know,  I had mine painted at a local shop for $50.00  there isn't that much area to paint!  and you have 1/4 of the work done already,  you have the headliner out  lol<BR>FD||||reg||1
